Mix ingredients and adjust pH to 7.0.  Distribute 0.9 volume of the medium into tubes (e.g., 4.5 ml of the medium in the Hungate tubes) under a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) gas mixture, seal with butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave.  <br>
To complete the medium, add the following stock solutions [Filter-sterilize NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution and store under a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) gas mixture.  The other solutions are autoclaved and stored anaerobically under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere] to the medium (per 4.5 ml):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 15% MgCl<sub>2</sub>&#183;6H<sub>2</sub>O solution                    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution                                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 2% Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution                      </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml        </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
